selection by email\")\n\n- [Tweet](https://www.fca.org.uk/news/press-releases/young-investors-trust-ai-more-tv-or-celebrities \"Share this selection on Twitter\")\n- [Facebook](https://www.fca.org.uk/news/press-releases/young-investors-trust-ai-more-tv-or-celebrities \"Share this selection on Facebook\")\n- [LinkedIn](https://www.fca.org.uk/news/press-releases/young-investors-trust-ai-more-tv-or-celebrities \"Share this selection on LinkedIn\")\n- [Share this selection by email](https://www.fca.org.uk/news/press-releases/young-investors-trust-ai-more-tv-or-celebrities \"Share this selection by email\")\n\nShare this selection\n\n- [Tweet](https://www.fca.org.uk/news/press-releases/young-investors-trust-ai-more-tv-or-celebrities \"Share this selection on Twitter\")\n- [Facebook](https://www.fca.org.uk/news/press-releases/young-investors-trust-ai-more-tv-or-celebrities \"Share this selection on Facebook\")\n- [LinkedIn](https://www.fca.org.uk/news/press-releases/young-investors-trust-ai-more-tv-or-celebrities \"Share this selection on LinkedIn\")\n- [Share this selection by email](https://www.fca.org.uk/news/press-releases/young-investors-trust-ai-more-tv-or-celebrities \"Share this selection by email\")","metadata":{"url":"https://www.fca.org.uk/news/press-releases/young-investors-trust-ai-more-tv-or-celebrities","ogUrl":"https://www.fca.org.uk/news/press-releases/young-investors-trust-ai-more-tv-or-celebrities","title":"Young investors trust AI more than TV or celebrities | FCA","og:url":"https://www.fca.org.uk/news/press-releases/young-investors-trust-ai-more-tv-or-celebrities","favicon":"https://www.fca.org.uk/themes/custom/fca/favicon.ico","og:type":"article","ogImage":"https://www.fca.org.uk/sites/default/files/media/images/fca_social_share.jpg","ogTitle":"Young investors trust AI more than TV or celebrities","cachedAt":"2026-09-21T03:00:58.119Z","language":"en-GB","og:image":"https://www.fca.org.uk/sites/default/files/media/images/fca_social_share.jpg","og:title":"Young investors trust AI more than TV or celebrities","scrapeId":"01a0c314-1ce3-717b-8043-895ede7c6958","viewport":"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0","Generator":"Drupal 10 (https://www.drupal.org)","proxyUsed":"basic","sourceURL":"https://www.fca.org.uk/news/press-releases/young-investors-trust-ai-more-tv-or-celebrities","cacheState":"hit","ogSiteName":"FCA","statusCode":200,"contentType":"text/html; charset=UTF-8","creditsUsed":1,"description":"Four in 5 less experienced investors have used AI for help with investing – and around two-thirds report doing so occasionally or regularly. ","theme-color":["#fff","#6c1d45"],"modifiedTime":"2026-08-27T09:00:42+01:00","og:site_name":"FCA","twitter:card":"summary","twitter:site":"@TheFCA","msvalidate.01":"57E38F6BD7138599EBD7F7F4FF496957","ogDescription":"Four in 5 less experienced investors have used AI for help with investing – and around two-thirds report doing so occasionally or regularly.","publishedTime":"2026-08-26T11:56:45+01:00","twitter:image":"https://www.fca.org.uk/sites/default/files/images/fca-logo-social-media.jpg","twitter:title":"Young investors trust AI more than TV or celebrities","funnelback:nid":"173371","og:description":"Four in 5 less experienced investors have used AI for help with investing – and around two-thirds report doing so occasionally or regularly.","MobileOptimized":"width","funnelback:type":"Press Releases,Consumer news","og:updated_time":"2026-08-27T09:00:42+01:00","twitter:site:id":"169431716","HandheldFriendly":"true","concurrencyLimited":false,"twitter:description":"Four in 5 less experienced investors have used AI for help with investing – and around two-thirds report doing so occasionally or regularly.","article:modified_time":"2026-08-27T09:00:42+01:00","funnelback:search-tag":"AI","article:published_time":"2026-08-26T11:56:45+01:00","funnelback:search-type":"main,foi,news","mobile-web-app-capable":"yes","funnelback:content-type":"News","funnelback:created-date":"26/08/2026","funnelback:modified-date":"27/08/2026","google-site-verification":"UMTpd8qXqUbCGtkijm3SkFV2lRJQM2lIIkMKmJg8jMk","funnelback:published-date":"2026/08/27","funnelback:published-year":"2026","funnelback:published-int-date":"20260827","funnelback:date-of-release-year":"2026","funnelback:historical-publication":"false","apple-mobile-web-app-status-bar-style":"black"}},"success":true},"pairedItem":{"item":0}},{"json":{"data":{"markdown":"We use cookies to improve your online experience. Some cookies are necessary to make the site work. We’d like to set additional cookies to understand how the website is used. These are optional. All cookie data is anonymised. View [cookies](https://www.fca.org.uk/privacy/our-use-cookies \"Our use of cookies\").\n\n- Functional\n\nThese cookies are necessary for the operation of the FCA.org.uk web site\n\n- Non-functional\n\nAccept analytics and campaign advertising cookies\n\n\nAccept additional cookiesReject additional cookies\n\n# EGR Wealth Limited enters administration\n\nNews storiesFirst published: 26/08/2026Last updated: 02/09/2026[See all updates](https://www.fca.org.uk/news/news-stories/egr-wealth-limited-enters-administration#revisions)\n\nOn 24 August 2026, EGR Wealth Limited (EGR Wealth) entered administration. Robert Goodhew and Geoff Bouchier of Kroll Advisory Limited were appointed joint administrators.\n\nThe joint administrators are responsible for managing the affairs of the firm during the administration process. They are officers of the court and need to comply with all insolvency law.\n\nEGR Wealth is authorised by the FCA. It provided discretionary investment management services, managed client investment portfolios, and facilitated the transfer and administration of client investments.\n\nOn 24 July 2026, EGR Wealth agreed to a [voluntary requirement](https://register.fca.org.uk/s/firm?id=001b000000NMalHAAT#what-can-this-firm-do-restrictions \"Restrictions: EGR Wealth Limited | Financial Services Register\") which restricted the activities it can carry out.\n\nBelow we set out for customers:\n\n- How to contact the joint administrators.\n- Information about the administration.\n- What to do if you are concerned about your investments.\n- What to do if you have a complaint with the firm.\n- How to protect yourself from fraudsters claiming to act on behalf of the firm, the joint administrators or the FCA.\n\n## Who to contact if you are a customer\n\nIf you have any questions, please contact the joint administrators.\n\n- Phone: +44 (0) 207 029 5078\n- Email: [EGR@Kroll.com](mailto:EGR@Kroll.com)\n- Website: [www.kroll.comLink is external](https://www.kroll.com/)\n- Address: Kroll Advisory Ltd, The News Building, Level 6, 3 London Bridge Street, London SE1 9SG\n\n## Support for consumers\n\nShow all\n\n\n### [Is the FCA overseeing the administration?](https://www.fca.org.uk/news/news-stories/egr-wealth-limited-enters-administration\\#expandable1921086)\n\nEGR Wealth is still authorised and supervised by the FCA. The firm must still comply with our rules.\n\nThe joint administrators are responsible for acting in the best interests of the people who are owed money by EGR Wealth. They must work as quickly and efficiently as possible.\n\nWe will continue to engage with the joint administrators and take any necessary actions to seek the best outcome for customers.\n\n### [What has happened to my investments?](https://www.fca.org.uk/news/news-stories/egr-wealth-limited-enters-administration\\#expandable1921091)\n\nEGR Wealth does not hold client money or custody assets. These are held by another regulated firm that keeps customers' assets secure in line with our rules. These rules are designed to protect client money and custody assets if the firm holding them fails.\n\nWe recognise many customers are concerned about their investments. The joint administrators are now in control of the firm.\n\nCustomers can speak to the joint administrators using the [contact details above](https://www.fca.org.uk/news/news-stories/egr-wealth-limited-enters-administration#contact \"Who to contact\").\n\n### [Do I need to do anything now?](https://www.fca.org.uk/news/news-stories/egr-wealth-limited-enters-administration\\#expandable1921096)\n\nIf you need urgent help with your account, [contact the joint administrators](https://www.fca.org.uk/news/news-stories/egr-wealth-limited-enters-administration#contact \"Who to contact\").\n\nYou should also get in touch if you have questions about income or withdrawals, need extra support, or want to discuss options.\n\nMake sure your contact details are up to date with EGR Wealth, using the [contact details above](https://www.fca.org.uk/news/news-stories/egr-wealth-limited-enters-administration#contact \"Who to contact\").\n\nThink about which firm you want to look after your investments in the future. Otherwise, the funds will not be managed and you may experience financial harm, such as your money under performing.\n\nCustomers who need free, impartial guidance about their finances can get help from [MoneyHelperLink is external](https://www.moneyhelper.org.uk/en \"Free and impartial help with money, backed by government | MoneyHelper\").\n\n### [I have made a complaint. What happens next?](https://www.fca.org.uk/news/news-stories/egr-wealth-limited-enters-administration\\#expandable1921101)\n\nIf you’ve made a complaint against EGR, you may be able to claim money that is owed to you.\n\nHowever, as it is insolvent, it will likely not have sufficient money to pay in full any compensation to customers where compensation is due.\n\nThis includes customers:\n\n- Waiting for a response to their complaint.\n- Who have received a final response letter from EGR Wealth with an offer of compensation but haven’t returned it.\n- Who have taken their complaint to the Financial Ombudsman Service.\n\nYou should first [contact the joint administrators](https://www.fca.org.uk/news/news-stories/egr-wealth-limited-enters-administration#contact \"Who to contact\") for more details about how complaints or claims will be dealt with.\n\nIf you’ve already referred a complaint to the Ombudsman, they will contact you in due course about next steps. You don’t need to take any action, but you can contact the Ombudsman if needed:\n\n- Phone: 0800 023 4567\n- Email: [complaint.info@financial-ombudsman.org.uk](mailto:complaint.info@financial-ombudsman.org.uk \"complaint.info@financial-ombudsman.org.uk\")\n- Website: [www.financial-ombudsman.org.ukLink is external](https://www.financial-ombudsman.org.uk/ \"Financial Ombudsman Service\")\n\n### [What is the FSCS and will it cover any losses?](https://www.fca.org.uk/news/news-stories/egr-wealth-limited-enters-administration\\#expandable1921106)\n\nThe Financial Services Compensation Scheme (FSCS) protects consumers when financial services firms fail.\n\nIt is the compensation scheme for customers of UK authorised financial services firms. It has eligibility criteria for which people and businesses are covered.\n\nThe joint administrators will work with the FSCS to decide next steps and will provide further updates.\n\nYou can contact the FSCS using the following details:\n\n- Phone: 0800 678 1100\n- Email: [enquiries@fscs.org.uk](mailto:enquiries@fscs.org.uk \"enquiries@fscs.org.uk\")\n- Website: [fscs.org.ukLink is external](https://www.fscs.org.uk/making-a-claim/failed-firms/egr-wealth-limited/ \"EGR Wealth Limited | Financial Services Compensation Scheme\")\n\n### [Do I need to use a claims management company or a law firm?](https://www.fca.org.uk/news/news-stories/egr-wealth-limited-enters-administration\\#expandable1921111)\n\nYou should proceed with caution if you are approached by a [claims management company](https://www.fca.org.uk/consumers/using-claims-management-companies \"Using claims management companies\") (CMC) or a law firm.\n\nFor the vast majority of clients, there is no benefit in involving a third party in reclaiming your assets.\n\nIf you use a firm such as this to assist in the return of your assets, they will likely seek a fee which may reduce what you get back.\n\nIf you are considering using a CMC or law firm to assist with the return of your assets, we suggest you first discuss this with the administrators using the contact details provided on their website.\n\n## Being alert to scams\n\nAll customers should remain alert to the possibility of fraud.\n\nIf you get an unexpected phone call from by someone claiming to be from EGR Wealth or Kroll Advisory Limited, end the call and contact the relevant party directly.\n\n[Find out more about protecting yourself from scams](https://www.fca.org.uk/consumers/protect-yourself-scams \"Protect yourself from scams\").\n\nPage updates\n\n02/09/2026\n: **Information added** within CMC section.\n\nWas this page useful?\n\nYes\n\nNo\n\nWhat can we do to improve pages like this?\n\nWhat did you find helpful?\n\nSubmit Feedback\n\nLeave this field blank\n\n[Print Page](https://www.fca.org.uk/news/news-stories/egr-wealth-limited-enters-administration/printable/print \"Print Page\")\n\n[Linkedin](https://www.linkedin.com/sharing/share-offsite?mini=true&url=https%3A//www.fca.org.uk/news/news-stories/egr-wealth-limited-enters-administration&title=EGR%20Wealth%20Limited%20enters%20administration&summary=&source=FCA \"Publish this post to LinkedIn\")\n\n[Twitter](https://twitter.com/share?url=https%3A//www.fca.org.uk/news/news-stories/egr-wealth-limited-enters-administration&text=EGR%20Wealth%20Limited%20enters%20administration&summary=&source=FCA \"Share this on Twitter\")\n\n[Share with Email](mailto:?Subject=EGR%20Wealth%20Limited%20enters%20administration%20at%20FCA&Body=I%20saw%20this%20on%20the%20FCA%20website%20and%20thought%20you%20might%20be%20interested%20https%3A//www.fca.org.uk/news/news-stories/egr-wealth-limited-enters-administration \"Share with Email\")\n\nShare page\n\n\n## [Related content](https://www.fca.org.uk/news/news-stories/egr-wealth-limited-enters-administration\\#relatedContentCollapse)\n\n[Protect yourself from scams](https://www.fca.org.uk/consumers/protect-yourself-scams)\n\n[Using claims management companies](https://www.fca.org.uk/consumers/using-claims-management-companies)\n\n- [Tweet](https://www.fca.org.uk/news/news-stories/egr-wealth-limited-enters-administration \"Share this selection on Twitter\")\n- [Facebook](https://www.fca.org.uk/news/news-stories/egr-wealth-limited-enters-administration \"Share this selection on Facebook\")\n- [LinkedIn](https://www.fca.org.uk/news/news-stories/egr-wealth-limited-enters-administration \"Share this selection on LinkedIn\")\n- [Share this selection by email](https://www.fca.org.uk/news/news-stories/egr-wealth-limited-enters-administration \"Share this selection by email\")\n\nShare this selection\n\n- [Tweet](https://www.fca.org.uk/news/news-stories/egr-wealth-limited-enters-administration \"Share this selection on Twitter\")\n- [Facebook](https://www.fca.org.uk/news/news-stories/egr-wealth-limited-enters-administration \"Share this selection on Facebook\")\n- [LinkedIn](https://www.fca.org.uk/news/news-stories/egr-wealth-limited-enters-administration \"Share this selection on LinkedIn\")\n- [Share this selection by email](https://www.fca.org.uk/news/news-stories/egr-wealth-limited-enters-administration \"Share this selection by email\")\n\n- [Tweet](https://www.fca.org.uk/news/news-stories/egr-wealth-limited-enters-administration \"Share this selection on Twitter\")\n- [Facebook](https://www.fca.org.uk/news/news-stories/egr-wealth-limited-enters-administration \"Share this selection on Facebook\")\n- [LinkedIn](https://www.fca.org.uk/news/news-stories/egr-wealth-limited-enters-administration \"Share this selection on LinkedIn\")\n- [Share this selection by email](https://www.fca.org.uk/news/news-stories/egr-wealth-limited-enters-administration \"Share this selection by email\")\n\nShare this selection\n\n- [Tweet](https://www.fca.org.uk/news/news-storie