://www.complianceweek.com/data-privacy/meta-reaches-18b-settlement-with-states-over-child-safety-violations/","cacheState":"hit","ogSiteName":"Compliance Week","statusCode":200,"contentType":"text/html; charset=UTF-8","creditsUsed":1,"description":"In-depth analysis and peer practice for 10,000+ risk and compliance leaders. HQP benchmarking, LPEC certification, and the ECI Compliance Week App included.","lwr-revised":"240.0","theme-color":"#fff","deployTarget":"CORE","modifiedTime":"2026-08-28T19:53:41+00:00","og:site_name":"Compliance Week","parsely-link":"http://www.complianceweek.com/data-privacy/meta-reaches-18b-settlement-with-states-over-child-safety-violations/","parsely-tags":"cw subscriber only,meta,tiktok,youtube","parsely-type":"post","twitter:card":"summary_large_image","og:image:type":"image/jpeg","ogDescription":"In-depth analysis and peer practice for 10,000+ risk and compliance leaders. HQP benchmarking, LPEC certification, and the ECI Compliance Week App included.","parsely-title":"Meta reaches $18B settlement with states over child safety violations","publishedTime":"2026-08-28T19:53:38+00:00","twitter:data1":"Oscar Gonzalez","twitter:data2":"2 minutes","og:description":"In-depth analysis and peer practice for 10,000+ risk and compliance leaders. HQP benchmarking, LPEC certification, and the ECI Compliance Week App included.","og:image:width":"2000","parsely-author":"Oscar Gonzalez","twitter:label1":"Written by","twitter:label2":"Est. reading time","og:image:height":"1333","parsely-section":"Data Privacy","application-name":"CW","parsely-pub-date":"2026-08-28T19:53:38Z","parsely-image-url":"https://i0.wp.com/www.complianceweek.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/11/metabuilding_605781-1.jpg?resize=150%2C150&ssl=1","concurrencyLimited":false,"article:modified_time":"2026-08-28T19:53:41+00:00","article:published_time":"2026-08-28T19:53:38+00:00","mobile-web-app-capable":"yes","msapplication-TileImage":"https://i0.wp.com/www.complianceweek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/compliance-week-icon.png?fit=144%2C144&ssl=1","apple-mobile-web-app-title":"CW","apple-mobile-web-app-capable":"yes"}},"success":true},"pairedItem":{"item":9}},{"json":{"data":{"markdown":"[![](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/images/728x90-Omnissa-banner-17-09-2026.jpg)](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/link.php?url=%20https://www.fstech.co.uk/autonomous-workplace-balancing-security-experience-and-control-in-financial-services/)\n\n#### Latest News\n\n- #### [Barclays staff push back against tighter return-to-office rules](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/Barclays_Staff_Push_Back_Against_Tighter_Return_to_Office_Rules.php)\n\n- #### [France ‘would back Dutch ECB president provided French chief economist elected’](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/France_Would_Back_Dutch_ECB_President_Provided_French_Chief_Economist_Elected.php)\n\n- #### [Revolut CEO says he wants dual UK-US listing for bank](https://www.fstech.co.uk/rs/Revolut_CEO_says_he_wants_dual_UK_US_listing_for_bank.php)\n\n- #### [Citi launches subscription management tool with Mastercard in UAE](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/Citi_Launches_Subscription_Management_Tool_With_Mastercard_In_UAE.php)\n\n- #### [Clarity Act fails to pass US Senate as Republicans turn on crypto bill](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/Clarity_Act_Fails_To_Pass_US_Senate_As_Republicans_Turn_On_Crypto_Bill.php)\n\n- #### [Revolut applies for Swiss banking licence, announces investment commitment](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/Revolut_applies_for_Swiss_banking_licence_announces_investment_commitment.php)\n\n\n[![](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/images/728x90-global-ai-awards-ofe-0926.gif)](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/link.php?url=%20https://www.nationaltechnology.co.uk/the-global-ai-awards/enter_the_awards.php)\n\n## London Stock Exchange trialling tokenised stocks with new partnership\n\nBy Isaac Hanson02/09/2026\n\nThe London Stock Exchange (LSE) is preparing to launch tokenised equity structures through a new partnership with the parent company of crypto exchange Kraken, the latest in a series of moves to modernise.\n\nThe LSE will work with Payward, which owns Kraken and is described as a unified financial infrastructure platform, to explore how it can create tokenised equity markets. The exchange said that this structure will be designed to broaden access to capital markets whilst preserving existing shareholder rights, protections and governance standards.\n\nThe two companies will collaborate on how best to connect the LSE’s regulated market ecosystem with digital-native technologies and wallet-based interactions, the exchange said.\n\nThis is the LSE’s latest push into the digital space, following programmes [including LSE 24](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/London_Stock_Exchange_To_Trial_Overnight_Trading.php), an all-day trading venue offering that the exchange described at launch as “near-continuous trading from Monday to Friday”.\n\nFrom next year, the Payward partnership will also offer retail investors the ability to trade tokens that track the share prices of public companies on the LSE 24. The LSE said that they will be directly linked to the value of public shares and move when they move, while adding the “speed, programmability, and around-the-clock access of blockchain”.\n\nJulia Hoggett, chief executive of LSE and head of digital and securities markets at the LSE group, said: “Tokenisation has the potential to change how investors access, and how issuers use, financial markets, but it must develop in a way that preserves the trust, rights and role of regulated markets.\n\n“By working with Payward, and continuing to collaborate across the market infrastructure ecosystem, we are exploring how issuers and investors can benefit from new forms of access while maintaining the standards that underpin public markets.”\n\n* * *\n\nShare Story:\n\n### Recent Stories\n\n### [Bank of America vice-president killed in Times Square stabbing](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/Bank_Of_America_Vice_President_Killed_In_Times_Square_Stabbing.php?utm_source=jsrecent)\n\n[READ STORY](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/Bank_Of_America_Vice_President_Killed_In_Times_Square_Stabbing.php?utm_source=jsrecent)\n\n### [Visa updates A2A Protect to prevent fraud before payments leave accounts](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/Visa_Updates_A2A_Protect_To_Prevent_Fraud_Before_Payments_Leave_Accounts.php?utm_source=jsrecent)\n\n[READ STORY](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/Visa_Updates_A2A_Protect_To_Prevent_Fraud_Before_Payments_Leave_Accounts.php?utm_source=jsrecent)\n\n### [London Stock Exchange trialling tokenised stocks with new partnership](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/London_Stock_Exchange_trialling_tokenised_stocks_with_new_partnership.php?utm_source=jsrecent)\n\n[READ STORY](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/London_Stock_Exchange_trialling_tokenised_stocks_with_new_partnership.php?utm_source=jsrecent)\n\n[![](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/images/Static-banner-728x90-01-09-2026.png)](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/link.php?url=%20https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/the-safeguarding-playbook/)\n\nCreating value together: Strategic partnerships in the age of GCCs\n\nYour browser does not support HTML5 video.\n\nAs Global Capability Centres reshape the financial services landscape, one question stands out: how do leading banks balance in-house innovation with strategic partnerships to drive real transformation?\n\n[![BANNER](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/images/300x250_FStech_cyber_conf_2025-Overview-1225.jpg)](https://www.fstech.co.uk/Online/FStechCyberSecurityConference-Overview2025.pdf)\n\n[![BANNER](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/images/TFOAI-overview-1225.gif)](https://www.perspectivepublishing.co.uk/dev/cms/uploads/FStech%20-%20Future%20AI%20Finserv/2026/fstechfutureofaiconference2025-overview.pdf)\n\nData trust in the AI era: Building customer confidence through responsible banking\n\nYour browser does not support HTML5 video.\n\nIn the second episode of FStech’s three-part video podcast series sponsored by HCLTech, Sudip Lahiri, Executive Vice President & Head of Financial Services for Europe & UKI at HCLTech examines the critical relationship between data trust, transparency, and responsible AI implementation in financial services.\n\nBanking's GenAI evolution: Beyond the hype, building the future\n\nYour browser does not support HTML5 video.\n\nIn the first episode of a three-part video podcast series sponsored by HCLTech, Sudip Lahiri, Executive Vice President & Head of Financial Services for Europe & UKI at HCLTech explores how financial institutions can navigate the transformative potential of Generative AI while building lasting foundations for innovation.\n\n- [Popular](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/London_Stock_Exchange_trialling_tokenised_stocks_with_new_partnership.php#solid-justified-tab1)\n- [Recent](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/London_Stock_Exchange_trialling_tokenised_stocks_with_new_partnership.php#solid-justified-tab2)\n\n- [1\\\\\n\\\\\nRevolut confirms customer data breach after fake government requests](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/Revolut_Confirms_Customer_Data_Breach_After_Fake_Government_Requests.php)\n- [2\\\\\n\\\\\nOpenAI launches ChatGPT for financial services](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/OpenAI_launches_ChatGPT_for_financial_services.php)\n- [3\\\\\n\\\\\nHSBC CFO Pam Kaur to step down](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/HSBC_CFO_Pam_Kaur_To_Step_Down.php)\n- [4\\\\\n\\\\\nMetro Bank launches new payments partnership to help businesses with cashflow](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/Metro_Bank_Launches_New_Payments_Partnership_To_Help_Businesses_With_Cashflow.php)\n- [5\\\\\n\\\\\nCrispin Odey loses appeal against City ban and £1.5m fine](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/Crispin_Odey_Loses_Appeal_Against_City_Ban.php)\n- [6\\\\\n\\\\\nWells Fargo commercial banking EVP set to retire](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/Wells_Fargo_Commercial_Banking_EVP_Set_To_Retire.php)\n- [7\\\\\n\\\\\nSenate Republicans introduce ethics text to Clarity Act on eve of vote](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/Senate_Republicans_Introduce_Ethics_Text_To_Clarity_Act_On_Eve_Of_Vote.php)\n- [8\\\\\n\\\\\nKlarna launches in-app call verification feature to fight fraud](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/Klarna_Launches_Inapp_Call_Verification_Feature_To_Fight_Fraud.php)\n- [9\\\\\n\\\\\nBarclays facing up to £37m bill over accounts provided to ‘Ponzi scheme’](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/Barclays_Facing_Up_To_37m_Bill_Over_Accounts_Provided_To_Ponzi_Scheme.php)\n- [10\\\\\n\\\\\nBarclays staff push back against tighter return-to-office rules](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/Barclays_Staff_Push_Back_Against_Tighter_Return_to_Office_Rules.php)\n\n- [1\\\\\n\\\\\nFrance ‘would back Dutch ECB president provided French chief economist elected’](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/France_Would_Back_Dutch_ECB_President_Provided_French_Chief_Economist_Elected.php)\n- [2\\\\\n\\\\\nCiti launches subscription management tool with Mastercard in UAE](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/Citi_Launches_Subscription_Management_Tool_With_Mastercard_In_UAE.php)\n- [3\\\\\n\\\\\nRevolut CEO says he wants dual UK-US listing for bank](https://www.fstech.co.uk/rs/Revolut_CEO_says_he_wants_dual_UK_US_listing_for_bank.php)\n- [4\\\\\n\\\\\nBarclays staff push back against tighter return-to-office rules](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/Barclays_Staff_Push_Back_Against_Tighter_Return_to_Office_Rules.php)\n- [5\\\\\n\\\\\nZopa launches AI banking assistant which uses natural language](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/Zopa_Launches_AI_Banking_Assistant_Which_Uses_Natural_Language.php)\n- [6\\\\\n\\\\\nRevolut applies for Swiss banking licence, announces investment commitment](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/Revolut_applies_for_Swiss_banking_licence_announces_investment_commitment.php)\n- [7\\\\\n\\\\\nClarity Act fails to pass US Senate as Republicans turn on crypto bill](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/Clarity_Act_Fails_To_Pass_US_Senate_As_Republicans_Turn_On_Crypto_Bill.php)\n- [8\\\\\n\\\\\nWorld Bank names Nobel laureate Michael Kremer as chief economist](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/World_Bank_Names_Nobel_Laureate_Michael_Kremer_As.php)\n- [9\\\\\n\\\\\nFCA seeking industry input on tokenising gold](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/FCA_seeking_industry_input_on_tokenising_gold.php)\n- [10\\\\\n\\\\\nKlarna launches in-app call verification feature to fight fraud](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/Klarna_Launches_Inapp_Call_Verification_Feature_To_Fight_Fraud.php)\n\n- [Expert Views](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/London_Stock_Exchange_trialling_tokenised_stocks_with_new_partnership.php#solid-justified-tabexpertviews)\n\n- [1\\\\\n\\\\\nFinance AI is about honesty, not personality](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/finance-ai-is-about-honesty-not-personality.php)\n- [2\\\\\n\\\\\nComplaint handling is the right place to put AI to work](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/expert-views-complaint-handling-is-the-right-place-to-put-ai-to-work.php)\n- [3\\\\\n\\\\\nShorten the path from financial statements to credit decisions – How AI is Closing the gap in commercial lending](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/shorten-the-path-from-financial-statements-to-credit-decisions.php)\n- [4\\\\\n\\\\\nBuild, buy or partner? Why the right AI strategy is the one built for your business](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/build-buy-or-partner-why-the-right-ai-strategy-is-the-one-built-for-your-business.php)\n- [5\\\\\n\\\\\nOpenAI Didn’t Fail at Checkout… Payments Did](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/expert-view-openai-didnt-fail-at-checkout-payments-did.php)\n- [6\\\\\n\\\\\nBuilding a Security First Culture in Retail Banking](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/expert-views-building-a-security-first-culture-in-retail-banking.php)\n- [7\\\\\n\\\\\nHow the CIO and CFO partnership has evolved in the digital age](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/how-the-financial-services-cio-and-cfo-partnership-has-evolved-in-the-digital-age.php)\n- [8\\\\\n\\\\\nBuilding the future of intelligent finance: Huawei’s vision for a digital financial ecosystem](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/huawei-building-the-future-of-intelligent-finance-expert-view.php)\n\nBeyond compliance: Building unshakeable operational resilience in financial services\n\nYour browser does not support HTML5 video.\n\nIn today's rapidly evolving financial landscape, operational resilience has become a critical focus for institutions worldwide. As regulatory requirements grow more complex and cyber threats, particularly ransomware, become increasingly sophisticated, financial services providers must adapt and strengthen their defences. The intersection of compliance, technology, and security presents both challenges and opportunities.\n\n[![](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/images/Finance-Ad-120x600-20260731.png)](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/link.php?url=%20https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/risk-resilience-and-the-modern-financial-workspace/)\n\n[![](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/images/120x600-FStechEvent-banner-17-08-2026.jpg)](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/link.php?url=%20https://www.fstech.co.uk/fsi-leadership-forum-navigating-ai-sovereignty-and-the-next-era-of-banking/)\n\n[![](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/images/120x600-A-rackspace-keep-control-ai-0526.png)](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/link.php?url=%20https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/scaling-sovereign-ai-across-uk-financial-services/)\n\n[![](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/images/payments-awards-book-now-120X600-Book-0726.jpg)](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/link.php?url=%20https://www.payments-awards.com/awards/booking_form.php)\n\n[![](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/images/120x600-FStechAI-Register-animated-0625.gif)](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/link.php?url=%20https://www.fstech.co.uk/futureai-finserv/)\n\n[![](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/images/120x600_FStech_cyber_conf_2026-register-now-0625.gif)](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/link.php?url=%20https://www.fstech.co.uk/cybersecuritylive/)\n\n[![](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/images/120x600-FStechawards2027-Open-animated-0826.gif)](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/link.php?url=%20https://www.fstech.co.uk/awards/enter_the_awards.php)\n\nWe use cookies to ensure you get the best experience on our website. [Learn More](http://www.perspectivepublishing.com/privacy_policy.html)\nAccept\n\n\n© 2019 Perspective Publishing     [Privacy & Cookies](http://www.perspectivepublishing.com/privacy_policy.html)\n\n![](<Base64-Image-Removed>)\n\n[To Top](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/London_Stock_Exchange_trialling_tokenised_stocks_with_new_partnership.php#)","metadata":{"url":"https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/London_Stock_Exchange_trialling_tokenised_stocks_with_new_partnership.php","name":"London Stock Exchange trialling tokenised stocks with new partnership","image":"https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/images/London Stock Exchange (1).jpg","ogUrl":"https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/London_Stock_Exchange_trialling_tokenised_stocks_with_new_partnership.php","title":"London Stock Exchange trialling tokenised stocks with new partnership - FStech","author":"Isaac Hanson","og:url":"https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/London_Stock_Exchange_trialling_tokenised_stocks_with_new_partnership.php","favicon":"https://www.fstech.co.uk/favicon.ico","og:type":"article","ogImage":"https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/images/London Stock Exchange (1).jpg","ogTitle":"London Stock Exchange trialling tokenised stocks with new partnership","cachedAt":"2026-09-21T08:25:11.141Z","keywords":"London Stock Exchange, Payward, Kraken, LSE, Julia Hoggett","language":"en","og:image":"https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/images/London Stock Exchange (1).jpg","og:title":"London Stock Exchange trialling tokenised stocks with new partnership","ogLocale":"en_GB","scrapeId":"01a0c315-1b7d-76b4-9522-e6f28def2ea7","viewport":"width=device-width, initial-scale=1","og:locale":"en_GB","proxyUsed":"basic","sourceURL":"http://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/London_Stock_Exchange_trialling_tokenised_stocks_with_new_partnership.php","cacheState":"hit","ogSiteName":"FStech","statusCode":200,"contentType":"text/html; charset=UTF-8","creditsUsed":1,"description":"The London Stock Exchange (LSE) is preparing to launch tokenised equity structures through a new partnership with the parent company of crypto exchange Kraken, the latest in a series of moves to modernise., The London Stock Exchange (LSE) is preparing to launch tokenised equity structures through a new partnership with the parent company of crypto exchange Kraken, the latest in a series of moves to modernise.","og:site_name":"FStech","twitter:card":"summary_large_image","twitter:site":"@FStechnology","ogDescription":"The London Stock Exchange (LSE) is preparing to launch tokenised equity structures through a new partnership with the parent company of crypto exchange Kraken, the latest in a series of moves to modernise.","twitter:title":"London Stock Exchange trialling tokenised stocks with new partnership","article:author":"Isaac Hanson","og:description":"The London Stock Exchange (LSE) is preparing to launch tokenised equity structures through a new partnership with the parent company of crypto exchange Kraken, the latest in a series of moves to modernise.","twitter:domain":"https://www.fstech.co.uk","twitter:creator":"@FStechnology","twitter:image:src":"https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/images/London Stock Exchange (1).jpg","concurrencyLimited":false,"twitter:description":"The London Stock Exchange (LSE) is preparing to launch tokenised equity structures through a new partnership with the parent company of crypto exchange Kraken, the latest in a series of moves to modernise."}},"success":true},"pairedItem":{"item":10}},{"json":{"data":{"markdown":"[![](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/images/728x90-Omnissa-banner-17-09-2026.jpg)](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/link.php?url=%20https://www.fstech.co.uk/autonomous-workplace-balancing-security-experience-and-control-in-financial-services/)\n\n#### Latest News\n\n- #### [Barclays staff push back against tighter return-to-office rules](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/Barclays_Staff_Push_Back_Against_Tighter_Return_to_Office_Rules.php)\n\n- #### [France ‘would back Dutch ECB president provided French chief economist elected’](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/France_Would_Back_Dutch_ECB_President_Provided_French_Chief_Economist_Elected.php)\n\n- #### [Revolut CEO says he wants dual UK-US listing for bank](https://www.fstech.co.uk/rs/Revolut_CEO_says_he_wants_dual_UK_US_listing_for_bank.php)\n\n- #### [Citi launches subscription management tool with Mastercard in UAE](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/Citi_Launches_Subscription_Management_Tool_With_Mastercard_In_UAE.php)\n\n- #### [Clarity Act fails to pass US Senate as Republicans turn on crypto bill](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/Clarity_Act_Fails_To_Pass_US_Senate_As_Republicans_Turn_On_Crypto_Bill.php)\n\n- #### [Revolut applies for Swiss banking licence, announces investment commitment](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/Revolut_applies_for_Swiss_banking_licence_announces_investment_commitment.php)\n\n\n[![](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/images/728x90-global-ai-awards-ofe-0926.gif)](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/link.php?url=%20https://www.nationaltechnology.co.uk/the-global-ai-awards/enter_the_awards.php)\n\n## Visa updates A2A Protect to prevent fraud before payments leave accounts\n\nBy Dalvinder Kular02/09/2026\n\nVisa has expanded its account-to-account (A2A) fraud prevention platform with new AI-powered capabilities designed to help financial institutions detect and stop fraudulent payments before money leaves customer accounts.\n\nThe enhanced version of A2A Protect introduces a new unified fraud score, marking Visa's first in-market integration of technology from Featurespace since [acquiring the fraud detection specialist in 2024](https://fstech.co.uk/fst/Visa_acquires_fraud_specialist_featurespace.php). The company said the update provides faster, clearer risk signals to help banks detect more fraud while reducing unnecessary alerts.\n\nVisa added that the launch comes as account-to-account payments continue to grow rapidly, with global A2A transactions projected to exceed 5.8 trillion by 2028, up 160 per cent from 2024.\n\nThe platform combines AI with transfer learning technology to give banks immediate access to fraud insights without waiting for models to learn from their own transaction data or for other financial institutions to join a fraud-sharing consortium. Visa said that banks that opt in can also access additional network-level signals to strengthen detection of emerging threats across the wider payments ecosystem.\n\nFor banks that choose to share network-level intelligence, A2A Protect highlights emerging scam hotspots and coordinated fraud activity that may be difficult for individual institutions to identify on their own. Visa said these insights provide an earlier view of risk and help identify scams before payment authorisation.\n\nAccording to the company, A2A Protect has increased fraud detection by 75 per cent during the first six months of deployment. Visa also said the enhanced platform can reduce more than 50 per cent additional fraud while cutting unnecessary fraud alerts by over 40 per cent.\n\nThe platform integrates with existing fraud systems through a single API, reducing implementation time and complexity. Each alert includes a plain-language explanation of why a transaction has been flagged, enabling fraud teams to investigate and respond more quickly while minimising disruption for genuine customers.\n\nJames Mirfin, head of risk and security solutions at Visa, said: “Fraudsters move fast across payment types, and financial institutions need risk insights just as quickly, without slowing down legitimate payments.\n\n“A2A Protect combines Visa's network expertise with Featurespace's technology to deliver a powerful new layer of protection that helps financial institutions detect more fraud, earlier.”\n\n* * *\n\nShare Story:\n\n### Recent Stories\n\n### [Bank of America vice-president killed in Times Square stabbing](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/Bank_Of_America_Vice_President_Killed_In_Times_Square_Stabbing.php?utm_source=jsrecent)\n\n[READ STORY](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/Bank_Of_America_Vice_President_Killed_In_Times_Square_Stabbing.php?utm_source=jsrecent)\n\n### [Visa updates A2A Protect to prevent fraud before payments leave accounts](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/Visa_Updates_A2A_Protect_To_Prevent_Fraud_Before_Payments_Leave_Accounts.php?utm_source=jsrecent)\n\n[READ STORY](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/Visa_Updates_A2A_Protect_To_Prevent_Fraud_Before_Payments_Leave_Accounts.php?utm_source=jsrecent)\n\n### [Andrew Bailey warns frontier AI could accelerate cyber threats to global financial system](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/Andrew_Bailey_Warns_Frontier_AI_Could_Accelerate_Cyber_Threats_To_Global_Financial_System.php?utm_source=jsrecent)\n\n[READ STORY](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/Andrew_Bailey_Warns_Frontier_AI_Could_Accelerate_Cyber_Threats_To_Global_Financial_System.php?utm_source=jsrecent)\n\n[![](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/images/Static-banner-728x90-01-09-2026.png)](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/link.php?url=%20https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/the-safeguarding-playbook/)\n\nCreating value together: Strategic partnerships in the age of GCCs\n\nYour browser does not support HTML5 video.\n\nAs Global Capability Centres reshape the financial services landscape, one question stands out: how do leading banks balance in-house innovation with strategic partnerships to drive real transformation?\n\n[![BANNER](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/images/300x250_FStech_cyber_conf_2025-Overview-1225.jpg)](https://www.fstech.co.uk/Online/FStechCyberSecurityConference-Overview2025.pdf)\n\n[![BANNER](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/images/TFOAI-overview-1225.gif)](https://www.perspectivepublishing.co.uk/dev/cms/uploads/FStech%20-%20Future%20AI%20Finserv/2026/fstechfutureofaiconference2025-overview.pdf)\n\nData trust in the AI era: Building customer confidence through responsible banking\n\nYour browser does not support HTML5 video.\n\nIn the second episode of FStech’s three-part video podcast series sponsored by HCLTech, Sudip Lahiri, Executive Vice President & Head of Financial Services for Europe & UKI at HCLTech examines the critical relationship between data trust, transparency, and responsible AI implementation in financial services.\n\nBanking's GenAI evolution: Beyond the hype, building the future\n\nYour browser does not support HTML5 video.\n\nIn the first episode of a three-part video podcast series sponsored by HCLTech, Sudip Lahiri, Executive Vice President & Head of Financial Services for Europe & UKI at HCLTech explores how financial institutions can navigate the transformative potential of Generative AI while building lasting foundations for innovation.\n\n- [Popular](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/Visa_Updates_A2A_Protect_To_Prevent_Fraud_Before_Payments_Leave_Accounts.php#solid-justified-tab1)\n- [Recent](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/Visa_Updates_A2A_Protect_To_Prevent_Fraud_Before_Payments_Leave_Accounts.php#solid-justified-tab2)\n\n- [1\\\\\n\\\\\nRevolut confirms customer data breach after fake government requests](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/Revolut_Confirms_Customer_Data_Breach_After_Fake_Government_Requests.php)\n- [2\\\\\n\\\\\nOpenAI launches ChatGPT for financial services](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/OpenAI_launches_ChatGPT_for_financial_services.php)\n- [3\\\\\n\\\\\nHSBC CFO Pam Kaur to step down](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/HSBC_CFO_Pam_Kaur_To_Step_Down.php)\n- [4\\\\\n\\\\\nMetro Bank launches new payments partnership to help businesses with cashflow](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/Metro_Bank_Launches_New_Payments_Partnership_To_Help_Businesses_With_Cashflow.php)\n- [5\\\\\n\\\\\nCrispin Odey loses appeal against City ban and £1.5m fine](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/Crispin_Odey_Loses_Appeal_Against_City_Ban.php)\n- [6\\\\\n\\\\\nWells Fargo commercial banking EVP set to retire](https://www.fstech.co.uk/fst/Wells_Fargo_Commercial_Banking_EVP_Set_To_Reti