https://www.fca.org.uk/news/blogs/better-outcomes-payment-firms-understand-customer-needs \"Share this selection by email\")\n\n- [Tweet](https://www.fca.org.uk/news/blogs/better-outcomes-payment-firms-understand-customer-needs \"Share this selection on Twitter\")\n- [Facebook](https://www.fca.org.uk/news/blogs/better-outcomes-payment-firms-understand-customer-needs \"Share this selection on Facebook\")\n- [LinkedIn](https://www.fca.org.uk/news/blogs/better-outcomes-payment-firms-understand-customer-needs \"Share this selection on LinkedIn\")\n- [Share this selection by email](https://www.fca.org.uk/news/blogs/better-outcomes-payment-firms-understand-customer-needs \"Share this selection by email\")\n\nShare this selection\n\n- [Tweet](https://www.fca.org.uk/news/blogs/better-outcomes-payment-firms-understand-customer-needs \"Share this selection on Twitter\")\n- [Facebook](https://www.fca.org.uk/news/blogs/better-outcomes-payment-firms-understand-customer-needs \"Share this selection on Facebook\")\n- [LinkedIn](https://www.fca.org.uk/news/blogs/better-outcomes-payment-firms-understand-customer-needs \"Share this selection on LinkedIn\")\n- [Share this selection by email](https://www.fca.org.uk/news/blogs/better-outcomes-payment-firms-understand-customer-needs \"Share this selection by email\")","metadata":{"url":"https://www.fca.org.uk/news/blogs/better-outcomes-payment-firms-understand-customer-needs","ogUrl":"https://www.fca.org.uk/news/blogs/better-outcomes-payment-firms-understand-customer-needs","title":"Better outcomes begin when payment firms understand customers’ needs | FCA","og:url":"https://www.fca.org.uk/news/blogs/better-outcomes-payment-firms-understand-customer-needs","favicon":"https://www.fca.org.uk/themes/custom/fca/favicon.ico","og:type":"article","ogImage":"https://www.fca.org.uk/sites/default/files/media/images/fca_social_share.jpg","ogTitle":"Better outcomes begin when payment firms understand customers’ needs","cachedAt":"2026-09-21T06:07:03.453Z","language":"en-GB","og:image":"https://www.fca.org.uk/sites/default/files/media/images/fca_social_share.jpg","og:title":"Better outcomes begin when payment firms understand customers’ needs","scrapeId":"01a0c315-b45a-77e0-b5b5-4cc8b3b5116c","viewport":"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0","Generator":"Drupal 10 (https://www.drupal.org)","proxyUsed":"basic","sourceURL":"https://www.fca.org.uk/news/blogs/better-outcomes-payment-firms-understand-customer-needs","cacheState":"hit","ogSiteName":"FCA","statusCode":200,"contentType":"text/html; charset=UTF-8","creditsUsed":1,"description":"Our review found that firms getting the best outcomes were taking simple steps to understand customers and vulnerability, and design support around them.","theme-color":["#fff","#6c1d45"],"modifiedTime":"2026-09-17T10:32:25+01:00","og:site_name":"FCA","twitter:card":"summary","twitter:site":"@TheFCA","msvalidate.01":"57E38F6BD7138599EBD7F7F4FF496957","ogDescription":"During our review of consumer vulnerability, we saw how relatively simple changes can make a real difference. One payments provider serving small business customers found that some customers were struggling to set up and manage their accounts because of limited IT literacy.The firm responded by arranging callback support to help customers set up their accounts.  As a result, customers were able to manage their accounts successfully, without needing to invest in expensive new systems or roll out elaborate new processes.","publishedTime":"2026-09-09T09:16:21+01:00","twitter:image":"https://www.fca.org.uk/sites/default/files/images/fca-logo-social-media.jpg","twitter:title":"Better outcomes begin when payment firms understand customers’ needs","funnelback:nid":"173846","og:description":"During our review of consumer vulnerability, we saw how relatively simple changes can make a real difference. One payments provider serving small business customers found that some customers were struggling to set up and manage their accounts because of limited IT literacy.The firm responded by arranging callback support to help customers set up their accounts.  As a result, customers were able to manage their accounts successfully, without needing to invest in expensive new systems or roll out elaborate new processes.","MobileOptimized":"width","funnelback:type":"Blogs,Firms","og:updated_time":"2026-09-17T10:32:25+01:00","twitter:site:id":"169431716","HandheldFriendly":"true","concurrencyLimited":false,"funnelback:category":"Firms","twitter:description":"During our review of consumer vulnerability, we saw how relatively simple changes can make a real difference. One payments provider serving small business customers found that some customers were struggling to set up and manage their accounts because of limited IT literacy.The firm responded by arranging callback support to help customers set up their accounts.  As a result, customers were able to manage their accounts successfully, without needing to invest in expensive new systems or roll out elaborate new processes.","article:modified_time":"2026-09-17T10:32:25+01:00","funnelback:search-tag":"Consumer Duty","article:published_time":"2026-09-09T09:16:21+01:00","funnelback:search-type":"main,foi,news","mobile-web-app-capable":"yes","funnelback:content-type":"Blog","funnelback:created-date":"09/09/2026","funnelback:modified-date":"17/09/2026","google-site-verification":"UMTpd8qXqUbCGtkijm3SkFV2lRJQM2lIIkMKmJg8jMk","funnelback:published-date":"2026/09/17","funnelback:published-year":"2026","funnelback:published-int-date":"20260917","funnelback:date-of-release-year":"2026","apple-mobile-web-app-status-bar-style":"black"}},"success":true},"pairedItem":{"item":16}},{"json":{"data":{"markdown":"We use cookies to improve your online experience. Some cookies are necessary to make the site work. We’d like to set additional cookies to understand how the website is used. These are optional. All cookie data is anonymised. View [cookies](https://www.fca.org.uk/privacy/our-use-cookies \"Our use of cookies\").\n\n- Functional\n\nThese cookies are necessary for the operation of the FCA.org.uk web site\n\n- Non-functional\n\nAccept analytics and campaign advertising cookies\n\n\nAccept additional cookiesReject additional cookies\n\n# Premier Payment Solutions Ltd enters liquidation\n\nNews storiesFirst published: 14/09/2026Last updated: 14/09/2026\n\nOn 10 September 2026, Premier Payment Solutions Ltd, which traded as PPS Money and MTBS (together, 'PPS Money'), entered liquidation. Bai Cham and Gary Shankland of BTG Begbies Traynor were appointed joint liquidators.\n\n## On this page ![](https://www.fca.org.uk/themes/custom/fca/images/document.svg)\n\n- [Who to contact](https://www.fca.org.uk/news/news-stories/premier-payment-solutions-ltd-enters-liquidation#section-who-to-contact)\n- [Information for customers](https://www.fca.org.uk/news/news-stories/premier-payment-solutions-ltd-enters-liquidation#section-information-for-customers)\n- [Being Alert to Scams](https://www.fca.org.uk/news/news-stories/premier-payment-solutions-ltd-enters-liquidation#section-being-alert-to-scams)\n\nPPS Money is registered as a small payment institution under the Payment Services Regulations 2017 (the PSRs). The firm provided money-remittance services, primarily supporting money service businesses to make cross-border payments, including through its network of FCA-registered agents, which are businesses or individuals registered to provide payment services on its behalf. [See a list of PPS Money’s current and former agents](https://register.fca.org.uk/s/firm?id=0010X00004eOZGxQAO#who-is-this-firm-connected-to-appointed-representatives).\n\nPPS entered liquidation after the directors determined that the firm could no longer continue trading. The joint liquidators are responsible for assessing customer claims against the firm and distributing funds back to customers where possible.\n\nIf you have any questions regarding the liquidation process, please contact: [premier.ps@btguk.com](mailto: premier.ps@btguk.com).\n\nWe will continue to engage with the joint liquidators and take any necessary actions to seek the best outcome for consumers.\n\n## Who to contact\n\nIf you have any questions, please contact the joint liquidators.\n\n- **Phone:** +44 (0) 1634 975440\n- **Email:** [premier.ps@btguk.com](mailto: premier.ps@btguk.com)\n- **Website:** [www.btguk.com/restructuringLink is external](https://www.btguk.com/services/restructuring)\n- **Address:** BTG Begbies Traynor, Unit F33, Innovation Centre Medway, Maidstone Road, Medway, ME5 9FD\n\n## Information for customers\n\n### [Why has the firm entered liquidation?](https://www.fca.org.uk/news/news-stories/premier-payment-solutions-ltd-enters-liquidation\\#expandable1931101)\n\nPPS Money entered voluntary liquidation after experiencing significant financial difficulties. The directors determined that the firm could no longer continue trading and resolved to place it into liquidation.\n\nThe joint liquidators will now manage the liquidation process and provide further information to customers.\n\n### [Is the FCA overseeing the liquidation?](https://www.fca.org.uk/news/news-stories/premier-payment-solutions-ltd-enters-liquidation\\#expandable1931106)\n\nPPS Money remains registered with the FCA and must continue to comply with our rules.\n\nThe joint liquidators are responsible for acting in the best interests of the people who are owed money by PPS Money. They must work as quickly and efficiently as possible.\n\nWe are liaising as appropriate with the joint liquidators.\n\n### [What should I do if I have money with PPS Money?](https://www.fca.org.uk/news/news-stories/premier-payment-solutions-ltd-enters-liquidation\\#expandable1931111)\n\nCustomers should contact the joint liquidators if they are concerned, have any questions or for any updates.\n\nThe joint liquidators will gather as much information as possible from customers of PPS Money about payments made to, or owed by, PPS Money.\n\nCustomers of PPS Money who believe that they are owed money by the firm should contact the joint liquidators using the contact details above.\n\n### [Are my funds protected by the Financial Services Compensation Scheme (FSCS)?](https://www.fca.org.uk/news/news-stories/premier-payment-solutions-ltd-enters-liquidation\\#expandable1931116)\n\nNo. The FSCS only applies to certain types of activity and does not cover payment services.\n\nPPS Money was registered as a Small Payment Institution under the Payment Services Regulations 2017. Unlike some other payment firms, Small Payment Institutions are not required to safeguard customer funds under the PSRs.\n\nCustomers should monitor updates from the joint liquidators for information about the return of funds and the claims process.\n\n### [Do I need to use a claims management company (CMC) or a law firm?](https://www.fca.org.uk/news/news-stories/premier-payment-solutions-ltd-enters-liquidation\\#expandable1931121)\n\nYou should proceed with caution if you are approached by a CMC or a law firm.\n\nFor the vast majority of clients, there is no benefit in involving a third party in reclaiming your assets.\n\nIf you use a firm such as this to assist in the return of your funds, they will likely seek a fee which may reduce what you get back.\n\nIf you are considering using a CMC or law firm to assist with the return of your funds, we suggest you first discuss this with the joint liquidators using the contact details provided above.\n\n## Being Alert to Scams\n\nAll customers should remain alert to the possibility of fraud. If you get an unexpected phone call by someone claiming to be from PPS Money, BTG Begbies Traynor or the [FCA](https://www.fca.org.uk/contact \"Contact us\"), please end the call and contact the relevant party directly.\n\n[Find out more about protecting yourself from scams](https://www.fca.org.uk/consumers/protect-yourself-scams \"Protect yourself from scams\").\n\nWas this page useful?\n\nYes\n\nNo\n\nWhat can we do to improve pages like this?\n\nWhat did you find helpful?\n\nSubmit Feedback\n\nLeave this field blank\n\n[Print Page](https://www.fca.org.uk/news/news-stories/premier-payment-solutions-ltd-enters-liquidation/printable/print \"Print Page\")\n\n[Linkedin](https://www.linkedin.com/sharing/share-offsite?mini=true&url=https%3A//www.fca.org.uk/news/news-stories/premier-payment-solutions-ltd-enters-liquidation&title=Premier%20Payment%20Solutions%20Ltd%20enters%20liquidation&summary=&source=FCA \"Publish this post to LinkedIn\")\n\n[Twitter](https://twitter.com/share?url=https%3A//www.fca.org.uk/news/news-stories/premier-payment-solutions-ltd-enters-liquidation&text=Premier%20Payment%20Solutions%20Ltd%20enters%20liquidation&summary=&source=FCA \"Share this on Twitter\")\n\n[Share with Email](mailto:?Subject=Premier%20Payment%20Solutions%20Ltd%20enters%20liquidation%20at%20FCA&Body=I%20saw%20this%20on%20the%20FCA%20website%20and%20thought%20you%20might%20be%20interested%20https%3A//www.fca.org.uk/news/news-stories/premier-payment-solutions-ltd-enters-liquidation \"Share with Email\")\n\nShare page\n\n\n## On this page ![](https://www.fca.org.uk/themes/custom/fca/images/document.svg)\n\n- [Who to contact](https://www.fca.org.uk/news/news-stories/premier-payment-solutions-ltd-enters-liquidation#section-who-to-contact)\n- [Information for customers](https://www.fca.org.uk/news/news-stories/premier-payment-solutions-ltd-enters-liquidation#section-information-for-customers)\n- [Being Alert to Scams](https://www.fca.org.uk/news/news-stories/premier-payment-solutions-ltd-enters-liquidation#section-being-alert-to-scams)\n\n## [Related content](https://www.fca.org.uk/news/news-stories/premier-payment-solutions-ltd-enters-liquidation\\#relatedContentCollapse)\n\n[Protect yourself from scams](https://www.fca.org.uk/consumers/protect-yourself-scams)\n\n- [Tweet](https://www.fca.org.uk/news/news-stories/premier-payment-solutions-ltd-enters-li